$ cc -h
usage: cc [options] file...      (.c compiled, .s assembled, .o .a linked)
  -o OUT      the output's name (default a.out; - with -S or -E: the screen)
  -c          compile (and assemble) to .o files only, no linking
  -S          compile to assembly (.s files) only, each statement's line above its code
  -E          preprocess only, to the screen
  -I DIR      look for #include files in DIR too (before /usr/include)
  -D NAME[=V] define a macro, as #define NAME V
  -lNAME      link the library /usr/lib/libNAME.a
  -s          leave the symbol table out of the program (smaller; db sees no names)
  -v          show each step's command
  -w          no warnings
  -h          this list
$ cc -S -o - hello.c | grep -c call
1
